  "id": "recurrent-circuit",
  "term": "recurrent circuit",
  "definition": "A recurrent circuit is a feedback loop in a neural system in which signals from principal output neurons return to earlier parts of the same network and influence later responding. In the source context, this refers to retinal ganglion cell signals feeding back through gap-junction-linked amacrine pathways to regulate the gain of visual responses.",
